---
const modules = [
  ['01','Market Map','Legal market, firm types, careers'],
  ['02','Read the Work','Practice areas, jurisdiction, economics'],
  ['03','Read Talent','Resume signals, ownership, motivation'],
  ['04','Run the Search','Intake, mapping, sourcing, outreach'],
  ['05','Close the Search','Offers, counteroffers, senior search'],
  ['06','Operate Well','Ethics, inclusion, AI, first 90 days'],
];
const testCheckoutUrl = 'https://recruitinglab.lemonsqueezy.com/checkout/buy/024bd629-dc0b-4d14-969a-cabbcdcca960';
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
  <meta name="description" content="A scenario-based learning experience for people entering U.S. legal recruiting." />
  <meta name="robots" content="noindex,nofollow" />
  <title>Legal Recruiter Lab — Playable MVP</title>
</head>
<body>
  <main>
    <nav class="nav"><a href="/lucas-capability-os-pages/">Capability OS</a><span>Experimental learning product</span></nav>

    <section class="hero">
      <div class="eyebrow">LEGAL RECRUITER LAB / PLAYABLE MVP</div>
      <h1>Learn to think like a<br/><em>legal recruiter.</em></h1>
      <p class="lede">Not another PDF to finish. A guided, scenario-based training path built from a 29-chapter professional learning guide for people entering U.S. legal recruiting.</p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="primary" href="#mission">Try a mission</a>
        <a href="#product">See the product model</a>
        <a class="test-checkout" href={testCheckoutUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Test checkout ↗</a>
      </div>
      <p class="test-note">TEST MODE ONLY · no live payments · do not enter a real card</p>
      <div class="proof"><span>6 learning paths</span><span>29 chapters</span><span>2 master cases</span><span>18 operator tools</span><span>90-day plan</span></div>
    </section>

    <section class="problem">
      <div><span>THE SHIFT</span><h2>From reading<br/>to operating.</h2></div>
      <p>The source guide already behaves more like a training system than a conventional ebook: it sequences the market, legal work, talent evaluation, end-to-end search execution, senior search, ethics and a first-90-days plan. The product layer turns those assets into missions, decisions, feedback and reusable tools.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="paths" id="product">
      <header><span>LEARNING MAP</span><h2>Six paths. One operator journey.</h2></header>
      <div class="pathgrid">
        {modules.map(([n,t,d]) => <article><b>{n}</b><h3>{t}</h3><p>{d}</p><small>LOCKED IN MVP</small></article>)}
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mission" id="mission">
      <div class="mission-head"><div><span>FREE MISSION 01</span><h2>Spot the real signal.</h2></div><div class="xp"><strong id="xp">0</strong><small>XP</small></div></div>
      <div class="case">
        <p class="case-label">CANDIDATE SNAPSHOT</p>
        <blockquote>“Assisted senior partner on multiple cross-border M&A transactions in the technology sector.”</blockquote>
        <p>What is the best recruiter response?</p>
        <div class="choices" data-question="q1">
          <button data-correct="false">Strong M&A fit. Advance immediately.</button>
          <button data-correct="true">Ask what the candidate personally drafted or negotiated.</button>
          <button data-correct="false">Reject: “assisted” proves the candidate lacked ownership.</button>
        </div>
        <div class="feedback" id="q1-feedback" aria-live="polite"></div>
      </div>
      <div class="case">
        <p class="case-label">CLIENT INTAKE</p>
        <blockquote>“We need a finance associate. The market is crazy busy, so good luck finding anyone.”</blockquote>
        <p>Which question creates the most useful search signal first?</p>
        <div class="choices" data-question="q2">
          <button data-correct="false">What law school ranking do you require?</button>
          <button data-correct="true">Busy doing what specifically — and is the work lender-side or borrower-side?</button>
          <button data-correct="false">Can we post the role nationally?</button>
        </div>
        <div class="feedback" id="q2-feedback" aria-live="polite"></div>
      </div>
      <div class="case">
        <p class="case-label">READINESS</p>
        <blockquote>“My staffing partner assigned me to a deal I did not want last month. It has been a rough few weeks.”</blockquote>
        <p>What should you test next?</p>
        <div class="choices" data-question="q3">
          <button data-correct="true">Whether this is a recurring structural issue or a temporary frustration.</button>
          <button data-correct="false">Whether the candidate will accept a 10% raise.</button>
          <button data-correct="false">Whether the candidate can start within two weeks.</button>
        </div>
        <div class="feedback" id="q3-feedback" aria-live="polite"></div>
      </div>
      <div class="result" id="result"><span>MISSION STATUS</span><strong id="status">0 / 3 complete</strong><p>Complete the three decisions to unlock your Operator Readiness score.</p></div>
    </section>

    <section class="model">
      <header><span>MONETIZATION DESIGN</span><h2>Sell outcomes, not pages.</h2></header>
      <div class="tiers">
        <article class="entry"><small>ENTRY · TEST PRODUCT</small><h3>Field Guide</h3><strong>R$119,99</strong><p>PDF + operator toolkit + quick-reference sheets.</p><a class="buy" href={testCheckoutUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open test checkout ↗</a></article>
        <article class="featured"><small>CORE · NEXT</small><h3>Operator Lab</h3><strong>Planned</strong><p>Interactive missions, scorecards, cases, progress tracking and certificate of completion.</p></article>
        <article><small>PRO · LATER</small><h3>90-Day Sprint</h3><strong>Planned</strong><p>Full lab + 90-day implementation path + AI practice prompts + portfolio-ready capstone.</p></article>
      </div>
      <p class="note"><b>Current validation state:</b> Field Guide checkout is connected in Lemon Squeezy Test Mode. The storefront remains hidden and live payments are not enabled.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="anonymous">
      <div><span>FACELESS BY DESIGN</span><h2>Brand-first.<br/>Operator-private.</h2></div>
      <div class="anon-grid"><p><b>Public:</b> product brand, curriculum, demo missions, learning outcomes, support alias, terms and privacy.</p><p><b>Private:</b> personal identity in marketing, video presence, personal social channels and founder-led sales.</p><p><b>Required:</b> payment processors and tax platforms may still require legal identity privately for KYC, even when customers only see the product brand.</p></div>
    </section>

    <footer><span>LEGAL RECRUITER LAB · EXPERIMENTAL MVP</span><span>Educational product · not legal advice</span></footer>
    <p class="flow-note">Flow note — This MVP connects the public learning demo to a Lemon Squeezy test checkout only. Live payments, storefront discovery and production delivery remain disabled until launch review.</p>
  </main>
<script is:inline>
  const answered = new Set(); let xp = 0;
  document.querySelectorAll('.choices').forEach(group => {
    group.querySelectorAll('button').forEach(btn => btn.addEventListener('click', () => {
      const q = group.dataset.question; if (answered.has(q)) return;
      answered.add(q); const ok = btn.dataset.correct === 'true';
      group.querySelectorAll('button').forEach(b => b.disabled = true);
      btn.classList.add(ok ? 'correct' : 'wrong');
      const fb = document.getElementById(q+'-feedback');
      fb.textContent = ok ? 'Correct — the discipline is to test the underlying evidence, not trust the label.' : 'Not quite — the next move should reduce ambiguity with job-related evidence.';
      if (ok) xp += 100; document.getElementById('xp').textContent = xp;
      document.getElementById('status').textContent = answered.size+' / 3 complete';
      if (answered.size === 3) document.querySelector('#result p').textContent = xp === 300 ? 'Operator Readiness: 100%. You consistently tested evidence before inference.' : 'Operator Readiness: '+Math.round(xp/3)+'%. Review the evidence-first pattern and retry in the full product.';
    }))
  })
</script>
</body>
</html>
<style is:global>
:root{--ink:#111;--paper:#f5f3ed;--line:#c8c5bb;--accent:#0d6b4d;--muted:#69675f}*{box-sizing:border-box}html{scroll-behavior:smooth}body{margin:0;background:var(--paper);color:var(--ink);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif}main{max-width:1500px;margin:auto;padding:0 28px}.nav{height:64px;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;border-bottom:1px solid var(--ink);font:700 10px ui-monospace,monospace;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.06em}.nav a{color:inherit;text-decoration:none}.hero{min-height:calc(100vh - 64px);display:flex;flex-direction:column;justify-content:center;border-bottom:1px solid var(--ink);padding:60px 0}.eyebrow,.paths header span,.model header span,.problem span,.mission-head span,.anonymous span,.result span{font:700 10px ui-monospace,monospace;letter-spacing:.08em;color:var(--muted)}h1{font-size:clamp(68px,10vw,150px);line-height:.82;letter-spacing:-.07em;margin:36px 0;font-weight:600}h1 em{font-style:normal;color:var(--accent)}.lede{max-width:800px;font-size:22px;line-height:1.4}.actions{display:flex;gap:12px;margin:28px 0;flex-wrap:wrap}.actions a,.buy{border:1px solid var(--ink);padding:13px 18px;text-decoration:none;color:inherit;font-size:12px;display:inline-block}.actions .primary{background:var(--ink);color:var(--paper)}.actions .test-checkout,.buy{border-color:var(--accent);color:var(--accent);font-weight:700}.test-note{margin:-12px 0 16px;font:700 9px ui-monospace,monospace;letter-spacing:.06em;color:var(--accent)}.proof{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;margin-top:28px}.proof span{border:1px solid var(--line);padding:8px 10px;font:600 10px ui-monospace,monospace}.problem,.anonymous{display:grid;grid-template-columns:.8fr 1.2fr;gap:80px;padding:100px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--ink)}h2{font-size:clamp(44px,6vw,82px);line-height:.94;letter-spacing:-.055em;margin:18px 0}.problem>p{font-size:19px;line-height:1.7;max-width:760px}.paths,.mission,.model{padding:100px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--ink)}.paths header,.model header{display:grid;grid-template-columns:220px 1fr}.pathgrid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);margin-top:50px;border-top:1px solid var(--ink)}.pathgrid article{padding:24px;border-right:1px solid var(--line);border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);min-height:210px}.pathgrid h3{font-size:28px;margin:45px 0 8px}.pathgrid p{color:var(--muted);line-height:1.5}.pathgrid small{font:700 9px ui-monospace,monospace;color:var(--muted)}.mission-head{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:end}.xp{text-align:right}.xp strong{display:block;font-size:72px;line-height:.8}.xp small{font:700 9px ui-monospace,monospace}.case{max-width:920px;margin:32px auto;padding:30px;border:1px solid var(--ink);background:#fbfaf6}.case-label{font:700 9px ui-monospace,monospace;color:var(--accent)}blockquote{font-size:24px;line-height:1.35;margin:22px 0;border-left:3px solid var(--accent);padding-left:18px}.choices{display:grid;gap:10px}.choices button{text-align:left;border:1px solid var(--line);background:transparent;padding:15px;cursor:pointer;font-size:14px}.choices button:hover:not(:disabled){border-color:var(--ink)}.choices button.correct{border-color:var(--accent);background:#e8f3ed}.choices button.wrong{background:#f4e8e6}.feedback{min-height:22px;margin-top:14px;font-size:13px;color:var(--muted)}.result{max-width:920px;margin:32px auto 0;padding:26px;background:var(--ink);color:var(--paper)}.result strong{display:block;font-size:32px;margin:10px 0}.tiers{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:14px;margin-top:50px}.tiers article{border:1px solid var(--ink);padding:28px;min-height:330px}.tiers h3{font-size:30px;margin:60px 0 14px}.tiers strong{font-size:42px}.tiers p{line-height:1.6;color:var(--muted)}.tiers .featured{background:var(--ink);color:var(--paper)}.tiers .featured p{color:#c9c7bf}.buy{margin-top:14px}.note{font-size:11px;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.6}.anon-grid{display:grid;gap:18px}.anon-grid p{margin:0;padding:16px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--line);line-height:1.6}footer{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;padding:30px 0 0;font:700 9px ui-monospace,monospace;color:var(--muted)}.flow-note{max-width:900px;margin:18px 0 0;font-size:10px;line-height:1.55;color:var(--muted)}@media(max-width:850px){main{padding:0 18px}.problem,.anonymous,.paths header,.model header{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:20px}.pathgrid,.tiers{grid-template-columns:1fr}.pathgrid article{border-right:0}h1{font-size:clamp(58px,18vw,100px)}.proof{margin-top:16px}.mission,.paths,.model,.problem,.anonymous{padding:64px 0}.case{padding:20px}footer{gap:20px;flex-wrap:wrap}}
</style>
